  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "A.Boopathiraja vs The Food Safety Officer on 21 November, 2024 Author: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Bench: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.(MD)No Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 21.11.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr. Justice G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.(MD)No.22250 of 2024 and W.M.P(MD)Nos.18803 & 18804 of 2024 A.Boopathiraja ...Petitioner -Vs- 1.The Food Safety Officer, Karunkulam, Seithunganallur Union Office Campus, Srivaikundam Taluk, Thoothukudi District. 2.The Designated Officer, (TNFS and DA department), Collectorate Campus, Thoothukudi District 628 101. 3.The Inspector of Police, Murappanadu Police Station, Thoothukudi District. ...Respondents Prayer : Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of Constitution of India for the issuance of a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamus, to call for the r relating to the impugned order Na.Ka.No. 3246/A2/2024 dated 06.09.2024 issued by the 2nd respondent and quash the same as illegal and consequen directing the 2nd respondent to remove the lock and seal and permit the petitioner to open his Gramuthu Virundu Hotel situated at Vasavapuram, Thoothukudi within stipulated time . https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Page 1 of 7 W.P.(MD A.Boopathiraja vs The Food Safety Officer on 21 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/142448943/ 1 For Petitioner : Mr.M.Perumal For Respondents : Mr.D.Gandhi Raj Special Government Pleader for RR1 & 2 Mrs.M.Aasha Government Advocate(Crl.side ORDER",
    "facts": "This writ petition has been filed challenging the order dated 06.09.2024, thereby sealed the premises of the petitioner's hotel on the ground that the petitioner is running the hotel without license and also sold banned tobacco products. While being so, on inspection, it was found that the petitioner had sold the tobacco products and seized 3 pockets of banned tobacco products. Therefore, FIR was registered in Crime No.72 of 2024 for the offence under Section 24(1) of the Cigarettes and Other Tobacco Products (Prohibition of Advertisement and Regulation of Trade and Commerce, Production, Supply and Distribution) Act, 2003 as against the person who was in occupation. , the second respondent inspected the premises and found that the petitioner has no license to run the hotel and also sold the banned tobacco products in the hotel premises. The FIR was registered as against the tea master and the petitioner is nothing to do with the tobacco products. The petitioner was granted license finally on 29.07.2021 and the same was valid upto 28.07.2022. Further, https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis FIR was registered as against the person who was in charge of the petitioner's hotel in Crime No.72 of 2024 for the offence under Section 24(1) of the Cigarettes and Other Tobacco Products (Prohibition of Advertisement and Regulation of Trade and Commerce, A.Boopathiraja vs The Food Safety Officer on 21 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/142448943/ 2 Production, Supply and Distribution) Act, 2003, on the file of the Inspector of Police, Murappanadu Police Station, Thoothukudi District and it is pending for investigation.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
